Inline object = new ref every render. React compare by ref, not value.

```jsx
// Bad — new object each render
<Child config={{ theme: "dark", size: 14 }} />

// Good — stable ref
const config = useMemo(() => ({ theme: "dark", size: 14 }), []);
<Child config={config} />
```

Also: wrap `Child` in `React.memo` or re-render still happen when parent render.

```jsx
const Child = React.memo(({ config }) => { ... });
```

Both needed. `memo` skip re-render only if props ref stable. `useMemo` make ref stable.
